      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to be skeptical; natural doesn't mean safe, and St. John's Wort is scientifically proven to interfere with birth control pills. This interaction is considered medically significant enough that doctors often specifically warn about it rather than dismissing it as minor. Because pregnancy can lead to serious health complications, I strongly recommend contacting your healthcare provider before using any supplement alongside this medication. Given your desire to avoid a quick doctor visit, checking with them immediately is the safest way to protect your reproductive health.",
